  "version": 1,
  "about": "Redaction vectors of the T-Agent browser extension (contract section 5). lib/browser-redact.js (server) and extensions/chrome/redact.js (extension) must both give these results. keys: keyIsSecret(name, value) for query, JSON and form names. headers: redactHeaders(headers). urls: redactUrl(url). bodies: redactBody(body, mime). json: redactJson(value).",
  "rules": [
    "A secret value becomes \"<redacted:N>\", N = the length of the original value (string characters; the digits of a number; the JSON text of an object or array).",
    "Names are split into words at separators and camelCase; the words author, authors, authored, authoring, authorship, coauthor, coauthors, authority, authorities are dropped; the rest, joined with \"_\", is matched with the contract pattern (case-insensitive).",
    "A whole number (a number, or 1 to 9 digits as text) under a name whose only matching words are \"tokens\" or \"sessions\" (max_tokens, total_tokens, sessions) is a count and is kept.",
    "Booleans and null are never redacted. A value that already is \"<redacted:N>\" is kept unchanged.",
    "Header names cookie, set-cookie, authorization, proxy-authorization are always redacted; other header names use the header pattern; a header value with \"Bearer <token>\" or a whole JWT is redacted.",
    "The headers referer, location, content-location and :path keep their URL with the query redacted.",
    "URLs: query parameters and a fragment of the form a=b&c=d are redacted by name, or when the value is a JWT. Values are written back as \"<redacted:N>\" (not percent-encoded), N = the length of the decoded value.",
    "Bodies: JSON (by mime or a leading { or [) is parsed, redacted and written back with JSON.stringify (compact); an urlencoded form (by mime or shape) is redacted like a query; other text is kept unless it is a whole JWT."
  ],
